/*
 * apprecorder.rc -- attaches res/apprecorder.manifest to whatever binary
 * compiles this file.
 *
 * Numbers, not names, on purpose: winuser.h spells
 * CREATEPROCESS_MANIFEST_RESOURCE_ID and RT_MANIFEST as MAKEINTRESOURCE(...)
 * macros, which rc.exe cannot evaluate in a resource statement. 1 is the
 * process manifest id (2 would be the isolation-aware DLL id) and 24 is
 * RT_MANIFEST.
 *
 * WHY A RESOURCE AND NOT link.exe's /MANIFEST: the linker's manifest tool
 * REPLACES resource #1 in the finished image. If both mechanisms are active the
 * generated manifest wins and this file is silently discarded -- no warning, no
 * error, just a process that is suddenly comctl32 v5 and system-DPI-aware. The
 * CMake block that adds this file therefore also passes /MANIFEST:NO, and
 * tests/test_ui_a11y.c asserts at runtime that the settings actually took
 * effect, so the two can never quietly drift apart.
 */
1 24 "apprecorder.manifest"
